      "costUsd": 0.0080615,
      "pronunciationText": "Last video ended here. On the left of the join, the gradient goes minus one, zero, one, and keeps rising, so the curve bends upward. On the right, it stays at two, and the line doesn't bend at all. So the bend comes from how the gradient changes. Now fill this vase from a tap, at a steady rate. The water level rises fast in the narrow base, slowly through the wide middle, then fast again in the narrow neck. So its graph bends down, then up. Where does the bend switch, and how do we measure it?"
    },
