      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 156,
      "outputTokens": 1222,
      "costUsd": 0.011076,
      "pronunciationText": "Inflection candidates are where f double prime is zero, or undefined. Here, six x minus twelve is zero at x equals two, so check that the sign really changes. f double prime of one is minus six, and f double prime of three is plus six. Minus to plus, so the concavity changes, and two, two is an inflection. So the cubic is concave down for x less than two, and concave up for x greater than two. Now compare y equals x to the fourth. f double prime is twelve x squared, which is zero at x equals zero. But it's positive on both sides. The curve is concave up all the way through, so there's no inflection at zero, even though f double prime is zero there."
    },
