      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 122,
      "outputTokens": 920,
      "costUsd": 0.008341,
      "pronunciationText": "The concavity also classifies stationary points. Back on our cubic, f prime is three, times x minus one, times x minus three, so the tangent is flat at one and at three. At x equals one, f double prime is minus six. The curve is concave down there, so it sits below its flat tangent, and every nearby point is lower. That's a hilltop: a local maximum, at one, four. At x equals three, f double prime is six. Concave up, so the curve sits above its flat tangent: a local minimum, at three, zero."
    },
