      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 156,
      "outputTokens": 1174,
      "costUsd": 0.010644,
      "pronunciationText": "But if f double prime is zero at a stationary point, the test can't decide. Look at these three curves: x to the fourth, minus x to the fourth, and x cubed. All three have a flat tangent at zero, and f double prime equals zero there. Yet one is a minimum, one is a maximum, and one is neither. So fall back on the signs either side. For x to the fourth, f prime goes minus, then plus: a local minimum. For minus x to the fourth, it's plus, then minus: a local maximum. For x cubed, f double prime is six x, which changes sign at zero. So the concavity changes at a flat point. That's a horizontal point of inflection."
    },
