      "pronunciationText": "y double prime is twenty x squared, times x minus three, so it's zero at zero and at three. Test the signs. At minus one, it's negative. At one, still negative. At four, positive. So the concavity changes only at three, and the only point of inflection is three, minus one hundred and sixty-two. Zero isn't one, because the sign doesn't change there."
