      "costUsd": 0.006039,
      "pronunciationText": "So now we have three graphs that work together: the curve itself, its gradient f prime, and the second derivative, f double prime. Their signs tell you where the curve rises, where it falls, and which way it bends. For our cubic, f prime is zero at one and three, the turning points, and f double prime changes sign at two, the inflection. Next: put all three together, to sketch a whole curve."
